# Regression: a blank line between two sibling pattern items (here a
# fact-level repetition followed by a fact) must not break parsing. The
# original parser had no `sep()` between items, so a blank line here trapped
# the parser (the trailing `ws()` consumed the blank line plus the next item's
# indent, leaving the item's content unconsumed -> parse error). The multi-
# line parser change added `sep()*` between items, fixing this.

a
b

$ rule two-items-blank
    (
        $( parse a )?

        parse b
    )
    ( both )
$ assert both
$ quit